{"final":false,"fragments":[[8,{"precedence":20,"provenance":{"tool_names":["build","edit_file","grep","judge","list_dir","read_file","write_file"]},"source":"tools_suite","text":"  read_file(path, offset=1, limit) -> line-numbered text ('<n>\\t<line>'); offset is a 1-based line. Output is capped at ~12 KB inline; if the file is larger, the tail is a marker '… <N> more line(s); read_file(path, <next>) for the rest' — call it with that <next> offset to page.\n  list_dir(path) -> directory entries\n  grep(regex, path='.') -> matching 'file:line: text' (a real regex, not a substring)\n  edit_file(path, search, replace, replace_all=false) -> surgical search/replace; `search` must match the file's exact bytes EXACTLY ONE place or it errors (add context to disambiguate, or pass replace_all=true to change every occurrence, e.g. a rename). Match file content only — do NOT include read_file's leading '<n>\\t' line-number prefix; keep `search` minimal (1-3 lines, just enough to be unique) (SIDE EFFECT)\n  write_file(path, text) -> create/overwrite a file (SIDE EFFECT)\n  build() -> compiles environment.c into the guest runtime: 'built' or the compiler's errors\n  judge() -> runs the probe over environment.c in w2m: the rows that differ from Windows's, or the item runs' verdicts once all are equal"}]],"history_ref":{"dropped":null,"from_seq":11,"to_seq":31,"tokens_before":4033},"results":[{"call_id":"c0","error":"","ok":true,"output":"1\t# Task: write environment.c for w2m\n2\t\n3\tw2m runs Windows x64 programs on macOS. It translates the program's x86-64 code and runs it inside\n4\ta virtual machine on Apple silicon. The program's kernel32 imports are served by a \"guest\n5\truntime\": freestanding C compiled for AArch64 with clang --target=arm64-apple-macos14 -O2 -std=c11 -Wall -Werror -ffreestanding -fno-builtin -fno-stack-protector -fno-exceptions -fno-unwind-tables -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables -mgeneral-regs-only, linked into the VM. There is no\n6\tC library: no memcpy, no memset, no headers but \"runtime.h\" (read it). Arguments arrive per the\n7\tMicrosoft x64 calling convention: the first four in the C parameters, and a fifth parameter `rsp`,\n8\twhen declared, is the guest stack pointer at the call (the fifth argument at *(u64 *)(rsp + 0x28)).\n9\tGuest pointers can be dereferenced directly. Each function's return value goes to RAX.\n10\t\n11\tWrite `environment.c` in this directory, defining exactly these functions:\n12\t\n13\t  u64 k32_GetEnvironmentStringsW(void);\n14\t  u64 k32_FreeEnvironmentStringsW(u64 block);\n15\t  u64 k32_lstrlenW(u64 string);\n16\t\n17\tThe process's environment block is the host's: UTF-16 entries, each ending in a NUL, then one more NUL,\n18\tat the address W2M_ENVIRONMENT_VA (an empty block is a single NUL there). runtime.h declares\n19\t  u64 w2m_heap_take(u64 size);          a process-heap block of exactly `size` bytes (HeapSize reports it),\n20\t                                        or 0 when the arena is full\n21\t  void w2m_heap_release(u64 api, u64 p); gives a block back\n22\tProbes see the process heap through GetProcessHeap and HeapSize, which use the same blocks.\n23\t\n24\tThe last-error code is w2m_teb()->last_error_value. Return from each k32_ function through\n25\tw2m_logged(W2M_API_<name>, arg0, return_value), which records the call and returns its third\n26\targument. Call w2m_unimplemented(W2M_API_<name>, detail) for an argument form you do not support;\n27\tit stops the run.\n28\t\n29\tThe judge runs the probe (probe_environment.c, compiled by Windows's clang) in w2m over your file, once per\n30\tcontract: contract-environment_set.json (environment block ['ZED=last', 'alpha=1', '=C:=C:\\\\w2m', 'SteamAppId=480', 'Path=C:\\\\Windows\\\\system32'], command line ending 'child-set'); contract-environment_empty.json (environment block [], command line ending 'child-empty'). Each contract's rows are what Windows printed on the runners; the probe's\n31\toutput in w2m must equal them exactly, row for row and field for field. Read the probe to see how\n32\teach contract's process is started (its command line and environment block).\n33\t\n34\tTools: `build` compiles environment.c and returns the compiler's errors or \"built\"; `judge` runs the\n35\tprobe over it and returns the rows that differ, or the item runs' verdicts once every row is equal.\n36\tWork until `judge` reports every item run accepted, then answer with one line saying so.","step":0,"tool":"read_file"},{"call_id":"c1","error":"","ok":true,"output":"1\t/* runtime.h — the w2m guest runtime's view of guest memory (Sprint 035).\n2\t *\n3\t * Freestanding C compiled to AArch64 and run inside the managed VM (BLACKBOARD 2026-10-09, runtime\n4\t * architecture). Addresses come from src/w2m/vm_backend.py as -D definitions: W2M_TEB_VA,\n5\t * W2M_PEB_VA, W2M_TRANSPORT_VA, W2M_RING_VA. Offsets are specs/guest_state.json's, confirmed on\n6\t * Windows in Sprint 034 (store/probe-runs/37989842529).\n7\t */\n8\t#ifndef W2M_RUNTIME_H\n9\t#define W2M_RUNTIME_H\n10\t\n11\ttypedef unsigned long long u64;\n12\ttypedef unsigned int u32;\n13\ttypedef unsigned char u8;\n14\t\n15\t/* TEB fields the runtime reads or writes (winternl.h and the Sprint 034 observations). */\n16\tstruct w2m_teb {\n17\t    u8 reserved0[0x08];\n18\t    u64 stack_base;                  /* 0x08 NtTib.StackBase */\n19\t    u64 stack_limit;                 /* 0x10 NtTib.StackLimit */\n20\t    u8 reserved1[0x30 - 0x18];\n21\t    u64 self;                        /* 0x30 NtTib.Self */\n22\t    u8 reserved2[0x40 - 0x38];\n23\t    u64 client_process;              /* 0x40 ClientId.UniqueProcess */\n24\t    u64 client_thread;               /* 0x48 ClientId.UniqueThread */\n25\t    u8 reserved3[0x60 - 0x50];\n26\t    u64 process_environment_block;   /* 0x60 */\n27\t    u32 last_error_value;            /* 0x68 */\n28\t};\n29\t_Static_assert(__builtin_offsetof(struct w2m_teb, client_thread) == 0x48, \"TEB ClientId.UniqueThread\");\n30\t_Static_assert(__builtin_offsetof(struct w2m_teb, last_error_value) == 0x68, \"TEB LastErrorValue\");\n31\t\n32\tstatic inline struct w2m_teb *w2m_teb(void) { return (struct w2m_teb *)W2M_TEB_VA; }\n33\t\n34\t/* Host transport: the runtime fills a request, executes hvc #8, and reads the result. */\n35\tenum { W2M_HOST_WRITE = 1, W2M_HOST_EXIT = 2, W2M_HOST_CLOCK = 3, W2M_HOST_UNIMPLEMENTED = 4,\n36\t       W2M_HOST_RUNTIME_FAULT = 5, W2M_HOST_FILETIME = 14,     /* 6-13: the file primitives below */\n37\t       W2M_HOST_MODULE = 15, W2M_HOST_PROC = 16, W2M_HOST_MODULE_PATH = 17, W2M_HOST_MODULE_AT = 18 };\n38\tstruct w2m_transport {\n39\t    u64 op;\n40\t    u64 arg[6];\n41\t    u64 result;\n42\t};\n43\t\n44\t/* Ring buffer: one record per service call, in order, for the first `capacity` calls; `per_api`\n45\t * counts every call by API id, past capacity too (Sprint 044: the hot services make millions of\n46\t * calls, and the totals must stay exact). The host reads both after the run, without an exit. */\n47\t#define W2M_RING_APIS 256                /* above every W2M_API_* id (tests/test_guest_runtime.py) */\n48\tstruct w2m_ring_record {\n49\t    u64 api;\n50\t    u64 arg0;\n51\t    u64 ret;\n52\t};\n53\tstruct w2m_ring {\n54\t    u64 count;                       /* records written, including any dropped past capacity */\n55\t    u64 capacity;\n56\t    u64 per_api[W2M_RING_APIS];      /* calls per W2M_API_* id */\n57\t    struct w2m_ring_record rec[];\n58\t};\n59\t\n60\t/* The thread's state block (specs/guest_state.json 0.2.0 state_block; Sprint 040). Translated code\n61\t * keeps the guest registers in host registers; the block holds them whenever the thread is not\n62\t * running x86 code: in a service, at a fault, when stopped. */\n63\tstruct w2m_state {\n64\t    u64 gpr[16];                     /* 0x000 rax rcx rdx rbx rsp rbp rsi rdi r8-r15 */\n65\t    u64 rip;                         /* 0x080 */\n66\t    u64 rflags;                      /* 0x088 materialized: CF PF AF ZF SF DF OF, IF and bit 1 */\n67\t    u64 flags_undefined;             /* 0x090 one bit per flag while undefined: C Z S O P A */\n68\t    u32 mxcsr;                       /* 0x098 */\n69\t    unsigned short x87_control_word; /* 0x09c */\n70\t    unsigned short x87_status_word;  /* 0x09e */\n71\t    u8 x87_tag_abridged;             /* 0x0a0 */\n72\t    u8 reserved0[7];\n73\t    u64 fs_base;                     /* 0x0a8 */\n74\t    u64 gs_base;                     /* 0x0b0 */\n75\t    u64 teb;                         /* 0x0b8 */\n76\t    u32 thread_state;                /* 0x0c0 */\n77\t    u32 suspend_count;               /* 0x0c4 */\n78\t    u64 af_operands[3];              /* 0x0c8 */\n79\t    u8 df;                           /* 0x0e0 */\n80\t    u8 reserved1[0x100 - 0xe1];\n81\t    u8 xmm[16][16];                  /* 0x100 */\n82\t    u8 ymm_high[16][16];             /* 0x200 */\n83\t    u8 st[8][16];                    /* 0x300 */\n84\t};\n85\t_Static_assert(sizeof(struct w2m_state) == 896, \"state block size (spec 896)\");\n86\t_Static_assert(__builtin_offsetof(struct w2m_state, rip) == 128, \"state.rip\");\n87\t_Static_assert(__builtin_offsetof(struct w2m_state, mxcsr) == 152, \"state.mxcsr\");\n88\t_Static_assert(__builtin_offsetof(struct w2m_state, af_operands) == 200, \"state.af_operands\");\n89\t_Static_assert(__builtin_offsetof(struct w2m_state, df) == 224, \"state.df\");\n90\t_Static_assert(__builtin_offsetof(struct w2m_state, xmm) == 256, \"state.xmm0\");\n91\t_Static_assert(__builtin_offsetof(struct w2m_state, st) == 768, \"state.st0\");\n92\t\n93\t/* Windows x64 EXCEPTION_RECORD and CONTEXT, at the offsets probes/guest_state measured on the\n94\t * runner (specs/guest_state.json windows.*). Only the fields the runtime writes are named. */\n95\tstruct w2m_exception_record {\n96\t    u32 code;                        /* 0 */\n97\t    u32 flags;                       /* 4 */\n98\t    u64 record;                      /* 8 */\n99\t    u64 address;     